x86_64-linux  the recorded rule in docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "An inline member function is a strong symbol": every constructor and destructor in this case is written inside its class, so clang emits only the form a use asks for and cxx1 emits both of Itanium's - the seven extras are cxx1's C1 and D1 forms and nothing clang wrote is missing or different. arm64-darwin agrees on all eighteen and the Windows comparison on all ten, which is where this case's question - which constructor each entry in the list reaches - is actually checked
